Reject a block switch in a stream that declares only one block type.

Backport of google/brotli@0ed4268a4401abcb4472096340477cf4af7d1a2b
("Detect and report invalid stream earlier"), which is not in any brotli
release yet (v1.2.0 is the latest tag). Node.js ships the same cherry-pick
for CVE-2026-111497 (nodejs/node@a6040b50d9, @49dff6f57a, @67d294739f).

Before this change the non-safe Decode{Literal,Command,Distance}BlockSwitch
wrappers were `static void`, so the fast path in ProcessCommandsInternal
ignored a failed DecodeBlockTypeAndLength and kept decoding with
inconsistent block state. They now return the error, and the stream fails
with BROTLI_DECODER_ERROR_FORMAT_BLOCK_SWITCH (-17, previously reserved).

Drop this patch when BROTLI_COMMIT moves to a release that contains
0ed4268a.

